From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:40:38 +0300
Subject: ETR_GL switches, no repeated glBindTexture, the HUD numbers in one
 draw

glfast.h: one environment variable per change (ETR_GL_TERRAIN, TUX, SHADOW, TRACKS, TREES, PARTICLES, SNOW, HUD, BIND), ETR_GL=0 turns all off, and the OpenGL 1.5 buffer functions the later changes use.

TTexture::Bind: SFML's Texture::bind is glBindTexture plus three matrix calls and a context lock; a texture that is bound already is left alone (the choice is forgotten at every frame, at beginSFML/endSFML and when a texture is loaded). The size of a texture is asked from GL once. DrawNumStr draws all characters of a string as one GL_QUADS.

